            <ArticleTitle>Modified dual guide catheter (&quot;ping-pong&quot;) technique to treat left internal mammary artery graft perforation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E28-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.25598</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Perforation of a left internal mammary artery (LIMA) graft during percutaneous coronary intervention is a rare event. We report a case of mid-LIMA perforation treated by a polytetrafluoroethylene-covered stent using a modification of the dual catheter (&quot;ping pong&quot;) technique. We propose that use of this modification when possible will further improve safety of treating a perforation.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2015 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
